{% extends "specification_user.jinja2" %}
{% block requirements %}
Create the Screen Function Specification in English. Use identifiers such as SCR-001, preferring existing source identifiers.

## Scope and Users
State the business activities, users and permissions, prerequisites, and scope.
## Screen Inventory and Navigation
List each screen's ID, name, purpose, users, display conditions, navigation origins and destinations, and launch method.
## Functions by Screen
For each display or input field, define its name, meaning, type, length and format, required status, initial value, editability, input constraints, validation timing, display conditions, and source of selectable values.
For each button or event, describe execution conditions, processing, successful displays and navigation, and failure displays. Cover search, lists, sorting, pagination, and similar functions when supported by the source.
## Integrations and Acceptance Criteria
Describe required external integrations and data inputs and outputs. If API or data details are undefined, record questions for later stages and cite identifiers only when they already exist.
For major operations, state prerequisites, actions, and expected results as acceptance criteria.
## Consistency and Open Questions
Identify source locations and unresolved screens, fields, navigation, and permissions.
{% endblock %}
